00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.050
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.860
We're leaving now.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:37.990
You listen to Ella and Tanaka, okay?

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:41.740
I'm sorry, Chris. Make sure you behave until we return.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:45.910
If I behave, will you come home right away?

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.830
Of course.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.540
Bye.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.720
I love you, Chris.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.010
I love you, Chris.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.650
If I behave, Mom and Dad will come home quickly.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.280
Chris!

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.330
They're presents from your mother and father.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.040
Wow! Look at it spin!

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.040
I believed them, but...

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:35.960
It never came true.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.290
Chuck?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.550
Thank you! I love you, Ella!

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.970
Amy!

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.720
Thank you for your hospitality.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.770
Goodbye, everyone. Take care!

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.730
Bye.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.700
Bye!

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.160
Goodbye, Cream.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.030
Goodbye, Amy.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.250
Goodbye, Tails.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.420
We're the only ones left, Sonic.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.550
Let's go.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:03.630
Okay.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:04.930
Sonic!

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:16.230
Be strong, Chris. Make sure you say goodbye.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.270
Be strong, Chris.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.400
Sonic.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.660
Chris.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.530
Take care.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.660
No...

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.160
It's been fun.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.630
No...

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.670
Thank you. Goodbye.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.470
No!

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.390
No!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.560
My dream for the future.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:04.450
My dream for the future is to be with Sonic forever.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.570
It sounds a bit childish.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.530
No!

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.460
Chris?

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.000
Chris?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.710
How could you!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.260
Sonic!

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.810
Chris!

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:42.000
Episode 51

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:42.000
Chris' Long Journey

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.110
Chris!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.670
Sonic?

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:10.340
Chris was very determined.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.390
Where's Chris?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.270
It's too dark to find him.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:22.650
Maybe we should go to Chris's favorite hangouts and see if he shows up.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.280
I feel that if we go after him, we're forcing him into a corner emotionally.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:33.120
But Sonic can't return to his world anymore.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.120
How can we atone for that?

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.040
Chris...

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.150
Where should we go?

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.570
Anywhere.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.440
We can't go home.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:11.110
Someplace far away...

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.800
Mom! My bicycle's gone!

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:33.510
I thought you threw it away because I bought you a new one.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.260
Oh yeah.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.270
Where should we go?

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.770
Anywhere you like, Chris.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.980
Okay.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.750
Seriously, where should we go?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.960
I said that anywhere is fine.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.420
I can't decide.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.000
Why not?

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.510
Because...

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:22.060
Is there a place that you want to visit, Sonic?

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.560
I already went to most places that I wanted to see.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:28.610
I see. You're right.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.990
You were always out and about.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.360
That's why I'm letting you choose, Chris.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.280
Okay.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.990
Are you okay with this, Sonic?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:36.950
About what?

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.030
It's nothing.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.620
We have a special report.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:51.550
Christopher, the son of Thorndyke Company's CEO Nelson Thorndyke, is missing.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:54.380
They've started a large-scale search.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:59.600
Chris! Hurry and come home!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.350
Chris!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.940
What are Mom and Dad thinking?

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.360
They're worried about you.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.360
I don't need them to worry about me!

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.950
These are the only times that they make a fuss!

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.240
They're so selfish!

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:24.290
Besides, I'm not the one they're looking for.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.850
My father sent them to catch us!

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.970
Chris, you give up?

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:45.930
No!

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:48.150
Okay! Wait a sec.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:05.450
I swear that I saw something.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:06.710
Hey!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.670
Please take us!

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.680
Are you sure you want to get off here?

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.810
Yes, thank you.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.980
Let's go.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.610
What's your world like, Sonic?

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:28.540
It's varied. I have various families and friends.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.160
Friends...

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:33.460
Yes! There are good guys and bad guys.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.420
They all lead their own lives.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.800
It's the same as this world.

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.050
Do you like it?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.390
I guess.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:54.520
Sonic, have you been here before?

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.940
Hmm...

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.940
You forgot.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:03.200
Because you're always running around everywhere.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.160
Probably.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.790
But I don't forget important things!

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:11.540
Really?

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:17.040
Yes, of course! When did you stop trusting me, Chris?

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.310
I wonder how everyone's doing.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:36.730
They're probably searching for us.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.230
But they'll never find us.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:44.110
They have no idea where we're going.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:47.370
Neither Mom nor Dad would know.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:49.740
Let's go.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:46.800
Chris!

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.930
Hey! Are you all right?

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:54.100
It didn't hurt! I'm fine!

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.810
I'm fine on my own!

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:06.900
Wow!

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.910
It's great!

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.540
You still haven't found them?

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.670
Widen the search area!

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.880
Contact the governor and get the police involved!

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:29.930
That's rght. Last month in the lab, we developed a wide-range detection system and an unmanned robot squad.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:34.060
Dispatch them all, no matter how much it costs!

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.810
I just remembered that I need to have food and presents ready for when Chris comes home!

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.770
Dear, please call the department store!

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.020
Right.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:47.190
Let's buy the toy section and have a party!

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:50.200
Chris, hurry and come home!

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.490
That's enough!

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:53.990
Father!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.750
Hang up the phone.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.420
Hang up!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.840
I was wrong.

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:08.920
I never blamed you for neglecting your household because you were too busy with work.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:14.010
That's because I also did whatever I wanted and continued my research.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:24.400
But I now realize that you've succeeded in your careers to give your son the best things possible.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:29.780
However, there are things that you can't get with money or power.

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:30.780
Father...

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.070
But Chris is missing, Father!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:40.750
Even without money and power, you should know where he's going.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:46.040
You should've spent more time with him.

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:51.970
In this whole world, you two are his only parents.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.300
Chris...

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.350
Lindsey!

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:06.730
A villa?

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:10.070
I came here with Mom and Dad a long time ago.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.320
I was really little back then.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.280
It's no good.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:22.500
We haven't used this place in years.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:27.210
There's a lock on the fireplace, and we probably can't use the oil anymore.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.260
Oops, I broke it.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.810
Sonic!

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:43.560
I brought some wood!

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.110
Are you all right?

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.980
Sonic...

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.570
I'll help you.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:57.240
It's okay. I can handle it.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.990
I see...

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.540
Why aren't you mad at me, Sonic?

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.580
It's my fault that you can't go home.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.630
Sonic.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:17.930
Isn't there something that you want to say to me?

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.680
Aren't you the one who wants to say something?

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:27.770
Sonic, why did you come with me?

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:30.150
Don't you have to go home?

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.440
You don't mind if I go home?

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.570
That's not fair.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:42.290
If I ask you not to leave, will you stay here forever, Sonic?

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:45.160
If that's what you want, Chris.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:48.960
Because you saved my life.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.670
Because I saved your life?

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.010
You're doing whatever I want because you feel that you owe me?

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:58.340
Chris...

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:03.680
Does that mean everything you've done is because you feel obligated?

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.440
A pool?

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.860
Water...

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:16.950
It's impossible.

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:45.700
Is that what it was, Sonic? It wasn't friendship?

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:50.960
Chris, friendship is free will.

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:53.210
Free will?

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:57.300
Neither I nor anyone else can make you choose how to feel.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.340
Only you can.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.050
Friendship is free will.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:07.260
So you're free to make your own choice.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:17.360
That means if I'm free to choose how I feel, then you're also free to choose how you feel.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:20.280
Or else, it won't be true friendship.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:26.410
Which world do you really want to live in, Sonic?

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.290
You finally asked the question.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:33.210
I don't care where I am.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.920
I have this.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.340
As long as I have this, I can go anywhere I want!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:44.340
But this place isn't good for you, Sonic.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.850
You didn't get a chance to run today.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:51.140
Because I can't keep up with you.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:55.100
I know that I'm holding you back.

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:56.860
It's my fault!

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.860
I'm the one who took away your freedom.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:04.740
I'm the one who's breaking up our friendship.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:06.530
It's my fault!

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:11.700
I can't be like you, Sonic...

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.380
Chris.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:22.210
If you leave, I'll be all alone again.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:33.350
I'll become a coward that can't do anything.

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.730
I disagree.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:43.440
You jumped into the pool in the middle of the night to save me.

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:47.200
I could never do something like that.

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:50.200
Sonic...

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:59.040
Chris, did you know that the moon is the same in both worlds?

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:09.590
Long time ago, you and I...

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:12.100
And when Chris was still little...

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:17.140
It was the only summer where we spent time together as a family.

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:24.280
Dear!

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:27.450
Chris?

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:33.740
Chris!

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:35.290
Chris!

